= Schema =

The V2 schema is intentionally small. It expands only when real content demonstrates a repeated need.

== Core semantic fields ==
Candidate baseline fields:
* Entity type
* Domain
* Epistemic status
* Related to
* Part of
* Implements
* Implemented by
* Supports
* Contradicts
* Derived from
* Source
* Verification date

Not every page requires every field.

== Entity types ==
Entity types describe what a page is about. The vocabulary should be derived from actual content and remain controlled. Likely recurring classes include:
* Concept
* Theory
* Model
* Method
* Project
* Implementation
* Organization
* Person
* Publication
* Dataset
* Software
* Protocol
* Species
* Technology

This list is provisional until the corpus mapping is complete.

== Domains ==
Domains are disciplinary or subject fields, for example Systems science, Biology, Computer science, Mathematics, Philosophy, Physics, Engineering, Economics, and Environmental science. Pages may belong to more than one domain.

== Scope ==
Scope is optional. Use it only for a meaningful boundary such as geographic, temporal, jurisdictional, organizational, experimental, system-level, or level-of-analysis scope.

== Semantic MediaWiki ==
SMW properties encode typed attributes and relationships. Property pages should document actual implemented properties, not speculative ones. SMW Concepts should be used for useful query-defined collections such as active projects or unverified theories, not as a replacement namespace for ordinary concept articles.

== Cargo ==
Cargo is complementary, not mandatory. Use it for repeated relational/tabular datasets where SQL-like aggregation and filtering are valuable. Do not mirror every SMW fact into Cargo.

== Templates and modules ==
Templates are interfaces to the schema: they normalize entry and rendering. Modules contain reusable logic when template code becomes too complex. Templates and modules must not become parallel ontologies.

